{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfi6DhYExEDaeuWM3EXa4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01U196e1tAm2DHabec82NxKX","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > docs/adr/ADR-007-client-templater.md <<'EOF'\n# ADR-007: Client templater with signal props, reactive regions, and mount\n\n**Date:** 2026-10-04\n\n**Status:** Accepted\n\n## Context\n\nThe hydration example scatters application state across component hosts.\nThe counter owns its own signal, the server hard-codes what it renders,\nand page behaviour is manual DOM code (query, listen, assign\n`innerHTML`). Authors coming from React or Preact expect one state\nobject, passed down, changed through named functions, with the DOM\nfollowing automatically.\n\nThe templater (`microtags/htm`) only runs on the server and returns a\nstring, so there is no way to describe a page once and have the browser\nbind it to state. ADR-004 says client bundle size outranks ergonomics,\nwhich would normally rule out a client-side templater.\n\n## Decision\n\nThe templater subpath gains a browser build, selected by the `browser`\nexport condition. The import specifier is the same on both sides; there\nis no runtime environment check.\n\n`html` returns opaque **markup** on both sides instead of a string. On\nthe server, converting markup to a string yields the HTML. Markup,\nrender output, and `raw` stay trusted strings, so nesting never\ndouble-escapes.\n\nOn the server, a signal or function in any hole is evaluated once. In\nchild position its output is wrapped in `<!--[-->` and `<!--]-->`\nmarkers, and so are children passed to a component. Function-valued\n`on<event>` props are omitted. A page with no reactive holes and no\ncomponent children produces the same bytes as before.\n\nIn the browser, binding depends on position: a signal as a component\nprop is assigned to the host's prop accessor; a signal or function as an\nattribute on a plain element binds that attribute (`false`, `null`, or\n`undefined` removes it); a signal or function in child position is a\n**reactive region**; `on<event>` with a function is a listener.\n\n`mount(container, markup)` adopts existing children without creating\nnodes, or creates them if the container is empty. It returns a dispose\nfunction. Mounting twice on one container throws. Adoption and\nreconciliation treat component hosts as opaque, entering only their\nmarked children range. Regions re-evaluate by a keyed morph: keyed\nchildren match by key, unkeyed children by position and tag name, and a\nmatching host is kept and rebound, never recreated.\n\nCore gains prop accessors on every host (read, assign a value, or assign\na signal to read through), picked up at upgrade if set earlier. Core\nalso exports `Signal` and `Serialized<T>` as types. `Serialized<T>` is a\nshallow unwrap; no runtime serialization helper ships.\n\nThis relaxes ADR-004 for the templater subpath only. ADR-004 still holds\nfor the core entry.\n\n## Trade-offs\n\nThe browser templater adds bytes that ADR-004 would otherwise forbid.\nThe cost is paid only by consumers who import `microtags/htm` in the\nbrowser; the subpath gets its own size-limit entry so growth stays\nvisible. The core entry grows by the prop accessors alone.\n\nChanging `html` to return markup is a breaking change. Every caller that\nneeds a string must convert explicitly. This is acceptable at 0.0.x.\n\nValue changes flow through signals with no diffing, but structural\nchanges are morphed, so a large keyed list re-evaluated often costs more\nthan a fine-grained list primitive would. Morphing keeps the API to one\n`html` function.\n\nOnce a signal is assigned to a prop accessor, the host's HTML attribute\nno longer tracks the value.\n\n## Consequences\n\nApps can keep one state object per page load, render the page from it on\nthe server, serialize it, and mount the same page over the server DOM in\nthe browser. Application code does no manual DOM work.\n\nComponent render links are still stripped (ADR-005). Creating a stripped\ncomponent in the browser throws an error naming the tag and pointing to\n`client: true` and the build-time keep list.\n\nADR-005 and ADR-006 get notes in follow-up work (return type, kept\ncomponents, second scaffold marker). No existing ADR is superseded.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/adr/INDEX.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"| [ADR-006][adr-006] | Authored HTML scaffold served by Hono | 2026-09-25 |\\n\",\n\"| [ADR-006][adr-006] | Authored HTML scaffold served by Hono | 2026-09-25 |\\n| [ADR-007][adr-007] | Client templater: signal props, regions, mount | 2026-10-04 |\\n\")\ns=s.rstrip('\\n')+\"\\n[adr-007]: ADR-007-client-templater.md\\n\"\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -c \"—\\|→\" docs/adr/ADR-007-client-templater.md; git add docs && git commit -qm \"docs: ADR-007 client templater\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":301,"cache_read_input_tokens":51607,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":301},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d20d9f1c-a441-44ac-9561-525ba24e77e3","uuid":"9fe818bd-249e-486d-a661-cbe71008c8e2","timestamp":"2026-10-04T23:48:29.726Z","request_id":"req_011Cfi6Dh8wNDmZd7JTmHVZk","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01U196e1tAm2DHabec82NxKX":{"command":"cat > docs/adr/ADR-007-client-templater.md <<'EOF'\n# ADR-007: Client templater with signal props, reactive regions, and mount\n\n**Date:** 2026-10-04\n\n**Status:** Accepted\n\n## Context\n\nThe hydration example scatters application state across component hosts.\nThe counter owns its own signal, the server hard-codes what it renders,